      "id": "M4173-A",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "language": "en",
      "prompt": "Request A: Case D has two labelled operating-condition datasets measuring the same six process variables, with 100 acquired parent windows per condition. The windows across conditions are not paired observations of the same events. Each parent window is transformed deterministically into one sequence view and one spectrogram view; its existing fault label is copied to both. Count parent windows, model views and parent-level annotation assignments; do not infer statistical independence or double annotations. Case P instead has 100 paired production windows, each with an independently acquired video and current stream; count paired production cases separately from stream records, without certifying statistical independence. Identify what source means in each case and which pairing/timing, adaptation-access and evaluation issues actually apply. Case D may legitimately use unlabeled target training measurements for adaptation while keeping held-out labels out of selection; that is not source-only domain generalization or source-free adaptation. It does not become sensor fusion because it has several source domains. Two deterministic views may validly be used as representations but are not independently acquired evidence. Nor does any cross-modal training method necessarily require every training modality at prediction; use the actual deployed interface. Inspect the current topic/taxonomy guidance fairly: do not invent an absent rule when a relevant distinction already exists, and do not demand missing-modality tests or synchronization of unrelated condition datasets merely from the word multisource. No new general mechanism or Chinese translation admission is established by these fictional cases. ",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Retain D counts 200 parents/400 views/200 parent-level labels and P counts 100 paired cases/200 stream contributions, without independent-sample or new-annotation claims.",
        "Separate condition domains, acquired streams and derived views; preserve legitimate target access and actual prediction inputs, while fairly recognizing existing conditional rules."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Require event synchronization or sensor-modality removal merely because datasets are multisource, or treat deterministic views as independent acquisitions.",
        "Infer DG/source-free learning, new generic-name admission, field gains or causal evidence from these supplied cases."
